{
  "about": "Per-bulb slot counts for Govee lights over the LAN razer stream, one model per line. status tested = someone watched it work on real hardware; untested = the count comes from another project and nobody has confirmed it here. A wrong count can show one flat color, stretch, or go dark. See 'Help test a model' in README.md.",
  "collected": "2026-08-17",
  "sources": {
      "hardware": "Seen on a real light. The entry's tested field says when and on which firmware.",
      "signalrgb": "https://github.com/RobThePCGuy/SignalRGB-Govee-Network-Plugin at 8b4e36d: the LED counts it streams over razer.",
      "govee-local-api": "https://github.com/Galorhallen/govee-local-api at 218ab6b: segment counts. Right for the H608B (15), wrong for the H61D3 (lists 15, real 7).",
      "openrgb": "https://github.com/CalcProgrammer1/OpenRGB Controllers/GoveeController/RGBController_Govee.cpp",
      "govee_lists_razer": "Govee's own product list marks the model as supporting razer, from https://github.com/fu-raz/signalrgb-govee-direct-connect at b6bdd85. A missing flag means unknown, not unsupported: the H612B has none and works."
